start language dictionary

type:logical operators

*-> !, not, revers    - reverse logic, example if (!a==a)->ret is NO, not condition
    -> exm:if (!a==a)->ret

*-> !           - expression of revers logic like not 
    -> exm:x!:->halt

*-> ()           - logical action of object 
    -> exm:(do)

*-> ()->         - nesting forvard operator
    -> exm:node()->inner

*-> *?           - comaprator with condition      
    -> exm:fun crt (file name="out.xml" alias xml ): -> open(file name="project.exe"):alias source:->extract(source *? data:type=dom to xml)   // extract all DOM elements in project.exe to out.xml

*-> -> or        - right strict link to node,dependence or relationship or other, example [model1]->[model2] or [node]->[fun]{act}
    -> exm:[a]->[b]

*-> /            - ordinary mathematical division operator (divide)
    -> exm:val b=y / e

*-> :            - true/false limiter and check; logical exist with Y/N, return Y/true if property exist or expression is valid, return N/false example lang:c++: wrt; null safe WITH ask - on N the logic halts and ASKS the human (see ask: when the check does not converge, the AI must ask, never guess)
    -> exm:lang:c++:

*-> :point:      - example of point for go to
    -> exm:goto::point:

*-> ;            - end of current function/layer/context do not use in prototypes or rules it is a marker of end context and clean token memory
    exm: 
        use dict src="VibeDSL" as data 
        -> crt file name="example.txt"
           -> type="xml":
              cnv data to xml
              append data
              save();     - end of logical block, marker of erase token logical data

*-> <            - left strict link to node, inverse node,dependence or relationship or other, example [file:text]<-[lng:eng]
    -> exm:val1 < val2

*-> <-()         - nesting backward operator
    -> exm:out<-()in

*-> <->          - two-way strict node,dependence or relationship, public function or interface and other, example [uroot con:lng]<->[usr:seq]
    -> exm:[a]<->[b]

*-> <>           - logical branching operator to a set: forks the logic into N parallel ways with their own results. : (the colon) is the true/false limiter and check - together <>: is variant logic where every way is checked Y/N, WARNING: <> is NOT "not equal" (unlike some languages) - for inequality use !=; any doubt about <> MUST be checked against the dictionary
    -> exm:a?<>:
       -> b
       -> c

*-> ==           - logical and mat equals of any object operator
    -> exm:a==b->run

*-> ?            - mapping marker of potentialy more way logic
    -> exm:exam?->show(variant(5))

*-> []           - block of entity or node, example [node:root]->[invoke delegate]>->[env:code] = "invoke delegate" or list params example [val1,val2,val3]
    -> exm:[val1,val2]

*-> \            - abstract change logic operator: applies an abstract change to a subject set: \(<subjects> act="add|delete|..."); \* is the filter form of this operator
    -> exm: \(file:name="dictionary.txt" act="delete")
    -> exm: \(stage 1:[file_abstracts,file_action,file_mapping,file_operators] action="add")

*-> \*            - logic filter operator: exclusion\*filtering by condition when applied inside brackets or quotes, example crt\*show - create without showing
    -> exm:crt\show

*-> as           - creates a variable/alias binding: expression + as + name makes the object available under that name
    -> exm: crt file="action.dict" as file_action

*-> brk, break   - break
    -> exm:switch(a) 
             case 1: 
             break

*-> case         - case
    -> exm:case val1: break

*-> cch, catch   - catch block marker, operator type action
    -> exm:cch:err
    -> exm:catch err

*-> continue     - continue: go on to the next iteration of the loop; the opposite of break
    -> exm:continue

*-> elif         - else if
    -> exm:elif(c==d)->ret

*-> else, els         - else
    -> exm:els:->ret

*-> end          - end
    -> exm:end:block

*-> exist          - exist
    -> exm:exst:file

*-> fin, finally   - finally block marker, operator type action
    -> exm: fin(close)

*-> for          - for example for(val1<0,incr(1))->data1=val1 -> for action

*-> goto         - go to point
    -> exm:goto::point:

*-> if           - if then else | if elif els - base logic operator to condition
    -> exm:if obj==obj | if a!=b
    -> exm:if(a==b)->ret

*-> is           - instanceof
    -> exm:obj is type

*-> none          - explicit absence of a value, logical operator: "here is nothing" Covers logical operators like :, req, -> with a way to state that a parameter is either not required or absent depending on reading context; unlike the ! marker it does NOT halt the logic, execution continues past an absent/not-required value
    -> exm:proto req(name) id="name" name-> blueprint id=name name=none

end language dictionary

*-> present , instanceof, belong - present, belong, instanceof, logical membership check condition 
    -> exm: file instanceof xml:->save()

*-> switch         - switch case action
    -> exm:switch:case val1: break

*-> switch, swt  - switch: branch selection by value, paired with case
    -> exm: :swt:type:case "action":

*-> try          - try block marker, operator type action
    -> exm:try:->logic

*-> unk, none, unknown - unknown, unknown state of required param. use this if param need entropy logic, or abstract  
    -> exm: data to file:name:none:map to mem

*-> when         - when: single conditional trigger, fires once when the condition becomes true
    -> exm: when(file:state:"opened"):close(file)

*-> while        - while: loop, repeat a block while the condition holds, condition is checked before each iteration
    -> exm: while(len>0):size-=1

*-> {            - start custom logic description
    -> exm:{do x}

*-> |, or         - logical or
    -> exm:a==b | a==c

*-> ||, and, &&  - logical and
    -> exm:a==b || c==d
    -> exm:a==b && c==d

*-> }            - end custom logic description
    -> exm:{...}

*-> ~            - logical mapping representation of any comparison expression
    -> exm: abstract if(obj~obj)
